1
00:00:01,439 --> 00:00:04,469
Last day.

2
00:00:04,469 --> 00:00:06,000
[Music]

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:11,520
Charlotte and Wilbur were alone. The families had gone to look for Fern.

4
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:14,000
Templeton was asleep.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:19,760
Wilbur lay resting after the excitement and strain of the ceremony. His medal

6
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:27,439
still hung from his neck. By looking out of the corner of his eye, he could see it.

7
00:00:27,439 --> 00:00:31,040
"Charlott," said Wilbur after a while.

8
00:00:31,040 --> 00:00:33,840
"Why are you so quiet?"

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:41,520
"I like to sit still," she said. "I've always been rather quiet." Yes, but you

10
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:49,359
seem specially so today. Do you feel all right? A little tired perhaps, but I

11
00:00:49,359 --> 00:00:55,439
feel peaceful. Your success in the ring this morning was to a small degree my

12
00:00:55,439 --> 00:01:03,600
success. Your future is assured. You will live secure and safe, Wilbur.

13
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:07,120
Nothing can harm you now.

14
00:01:07,120 --> 00:01:12,398
These autumn days will shorten and grow cold. The leaves will shake loose from

15
00:01:12,398 --> 00:01:19,279
the trees and fall. Christmas will come, then the snows of winter. You will live

16
00:01:19,279 --> 00:01:25,439
to enjoy the beauty of the frozen world, for you mean a great deal to Zuckerman,

17
00:01:25,439 --> 00:01:32,079
and he will not harm you ever. Winter will pass, the days will lengthen, the

18
00:01:32,079 --> 00:01:36,318
ice will melt in the pasture pond.

19
00:01:36,318 --> 00:01:39,120
The song sparrow will return and sing.

20
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:45,840
The frogs will awake. The warm wind will blow again. All these sights and sounds

21
00:01:45,840 --> 00:01:54,079
and smells will be yours to enjoy, Wilbur. This lovely world, these precious days.

22
00:01:54,079 --> 00:02:00,159
Charlotte stopped. A moment later, a tear came to Wilbur's eye. Oh,

23
00:02:00,159 --> 00:02:06,719
Charlotte, he said, to think that when I first met you, I thought you were cruel

24
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:10,238
and bloodthirsty.

25
00:02:10,238 --> 00:02:15,200
When he recovered from his emotion, he spoke again. "Why did you do all this

26
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:19,120
for me?" he asked. "I don't deserve it.

27
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:24,959
I've never done anything for you." "You have been my friend," replied Charlotte.

28
00:02:24,959 --> 00:02:33,279
"That in itself is a tremendous thing. I wo my webs for you because I liked you.

29
00:02:33,279 --> 00:02:42,159
After all, what's a life anyway? We're born, we live a little while, we die.

30
00:02:42,159 --> 00:02:46,238
A spider's life can't help being something of a mess. With all this

31
00:02:46,238 --> 00:02:52,159
trapping and eating flies by helping you, perhaps I was trying to lift up my

32
00:02:52,159 --> 00:02:57,920
life a trifle. Heaven knows anyone's life can stand a little of that.

33
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:04,639
Well, said Wilbur, I'm no good at making speeches. I haven't got your gift for

34
00:03:04,639 --> 00:03:09,120
words. But you have saved me, Charlotte.

35
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:12,398
And I would gladly give my life for you.

36
00:03:12,398 --> 00:03:15,760
I really would.

37
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:21,120
I'm sure you would, and I thank you for your generous sentiments,

38
00:03:21,120 --> 00:03:27,920
Charlotte, said Wilbur. We're all going home today. The fair is almost over.

39
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:32,559
Won't it be wonderful to be back home in the barn cellar again with the sheep and

40
00:03:32,559 --> 00:03:37,920
the geese? Aren't you anxious to get home? For a moment, Charlotte said

41
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:46,000
nothing. Then she spoke in a voice so low could hardly hear the words.

42
00:03:46,000 --> 00:03:52,559
"I will not be going back to the barn," she said. Wilbur leapt to his feet. "Not

43
00:03:52,559 --> 00:03:59,279
going back," he cried. Charlotte, what are you talking about? I'm done for,"

44
00:03:59,279 --> 00:04:05,680
she replied. "In a day or two, I'll be dead. I haven't even strength enough to

45
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:11,040
climb down into the crate. I doubt if I have enough silk in my spinets to lower

46
00:04:11,040 --> 00:04:14,318
me to the ground."

47
00:04:14,318 --> 00:04:20,959
Hearing this, Wilbur threw himself down in an agony of pain and sorrow. Great

48
00:04:20,959 --> 00:04:27,359
sobs racked his body. He heaved and grunted with desolation.

49
00:04:27,359 --> 00:04:36,079
Charlotte, he moaned. Charlotte, my true friend. Come now, let's not make a

50
00:04:36,079 --> 00:04:42,639
scene, said the spider. Be quiet, Wilbur. Stop thrashing about.

51
00:04:42,639 --> 00:04:49,279
But I can't stand it, shouted Wilbur. I won't leave you here alone to die. If

52
00:04:49,279 --> 00:04:54,398
you're going to stay here, I shall stay, too.

53
00:04:54,639 --> 00:05:01,840
Don't be ridiculous, said Charlotte. You can't stay here. Zuckerman and Lurvy and

54
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:06,079
John Arable and the others will be back any minute now, and they'll shove you

55
00:05:06,079 --> 00:05:08,799
into that crate, and away you'll go.

56
00:05:08,799 --> 00:05:14,398
Besides, it wouldn't make any sense for you to stay. There would be no one to

57
00:05:14,398 --> 00:05:20,799
feed you. The fairgrounds will soon be empty and deserted.

58
00:05:20,799 --> 00:05:27,439
Wilbur was in a panic. He raced round and round the pin. Suddenly, he had an

59
00:05:27,439 --> 00:05:33,120
idea. He thought of the egg sack and the 514 little spiders that would hatch in

60
00:05:33,120 --> 00:05:38,879
the spring. If Charlotte herself was unable to go home to the barn, at least

61
00:05:38,879 --> 00:05:42,799
he must take her children along.

62
00:05:42,799 --> 00:05:45,439
Wilbur rushed to the front of his pin.

63
00:05:45,439 --> 00:05:50,398
He put his front feet up on the top board and gazed around. In the distance

64
00:05:50,398 --> 00:05:54,000
he saw the arables and the Zuckermanman's approaching. He knew he

65
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:59,680
would have to act quickly. "Where's Templeton?" he demanded. "He's in that

66
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:05,199
corner under the straw, asleep," said Charlotte. Wilbur rushed over, pushed

67
00:06:05,199 --> 00:06:10,799
his strong snout under the rat, and tossed him into the air.

68
00:06:10,799 --> 00:06:15,120
"Tippleton!" screamed Wilbur. Pay attention.

69
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:22,079
The rat, surprised out of a sound sleep, looked first dazed, then disgusted.

70
00:06:22,079 --> 00:06:28,799
"What kind of monkey shine is this?" he growled. "Can't the rat catch a wink of

71
00:06:28,799 --> 00:06:34,719
sleep without being rudely popped into the air?" "Listen to me," cried Wilbur.

72
00:06:34,719 --> 00:06:41,120
"Sharot is very ill. She has only a short time to live. She cannot accompany

73
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:45,199
us home because of her condition.

74
00:06:45,199 --> 00:06:51,120
Therefore, it is absolutely necessary that I take her exac with me. I can't

75
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:57,279
reach it and I can't climb. You are the only one that can get it. There's not a

76
00:06:57,279 --> 00:07:01,840
second to be lost. The people are coming. They'll be here in no time.

77
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:08,559
Please, please, please, Templeton, climb up and get the egg sack.

78
00:07:08,559 --> 00:07:15,760
The rat yawned. He straightened his whiskers. Then he looked up at the egg

79
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:20,238
sack. "So he said in disgust."

80
00:07:20,238 --> 00:07:27,199
"So it's old Templeton to the rescue again. Is it Templeton? Do this.

81
00:07:27,199 --> 00:07:32,079
Templeton, do that. Templeton, please run down to the dump and get me a

82
00:07:32,079 --> 00:07:38,159
magazine clipping. Templeton, please lend me a piece of string so I can spin a web."

83
00:07:38,159 --> 00:07:44,719
Oh, hurry, said Wilbur. Hurry up, Templeton.

84
00:07:44,719 --> 00:07:52,959
But the rat was in no hurry. He began imitating Wilbur's voice. So, it's Hurry

85
00:07:52,959 --> 00:08:00,959
up, Templeton. Is it? He said, "And what thanks do I ever get for these

86
00:08:00,959 --> 00:08:08,079
services? I would like to know." Never a kind word for old Templeton. only abuse

87
00:08:08,079 --> 00:08:16,559
and wise cracks and side remarks. Never a kind word for a rat.

88
00:08:16,559 --> 00:08:24,719
Templeton, said Wilbur in desperation, if you don't stop talking and get busy, all will be

89
00:08:24,719 --> 00:08:28,879
lost, and I will die of a broken heart.

90
00:08:28,879 --> 00:08:37,279
Please climb up." Templeton lay back in the straw. Lazily, he placed his foraws

91
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:45,199
behind his head and crossed his knees in an attitude of complete relaxation.

92
00:08:45,199 --> 00:08:48,799
"I have a broken heart," he mimicked.

93
00:08:48,799 --> 00:08:54,719
"How touching! My I noticed that it's always me you come

94
00:08:54,719 --> 00:08:59,520
to when in trouble, but I have never heard of anyone's heartbreaking on my

95
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:04,959
account." Oh, no. Who cares anything about old Templeton?

96
00:09:04,959 --> 00:09:13,439
Get up, screamed Wilbur. Stop acting like a spoiled child.

97
00:09:13,439 --> 00:09:19,439
Templeton grinned and lay still. Who made trip after trip to the dump? He

98
00:09:19,439 --> 00:09:26,238
asked. Why, it was old Templeton who saved Charlotte's life by scaring that

99
00:09:26,238 --> 00:09:29,279
arable boy away with a rotten goose egg.

100
00:09:29,279 --> 00:09:34,879
Bless my soul. I believe it was old Templeton. Who bit your tail and got you

101
00:09:34,879 --> 00:09:42,279
back on your feet this morning after you had fainted in front of the crowd? Old Templeton?

102
00:09:42,318 --> 00:09:46,639
Has it ever occurred to you that I'm sick of running errands and doing

103
00:09:46,639 --> 00:09:52,159
favors? What do you think I am anyway? A rat of Volwick?

104
00:09:52,159 --> 00:09:58,000
Wilbur was desperate. The people were coming and the rat was failing him.

105
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:04,079
Suddenly, he remembered Templeton's fondness for food. "Timultton," he said,

106
00:10:04,079 --> 00:10:08,398
"I will make you a solemn promise.

107
00:10:08,398 --> 00:10:14,318
"Get Charlotte's egg sack for me, and from now on, I will let you eat first

108
00:10:14,318 --> 00:10:20,000
when Lurvy slops me. I will let you have your choice of everything in the trough,

109
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:27,040
and I won't touch a thing until you're through." The rat sat up. You mean that?

110
00:10:27,040 --> 00:10:31,840
He said, "I promise I cross my heart."

111
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:35,359
"All right, it's a deal," said the rat.

112
00:10:35,359 --> 00:10:39,600
He walked to the wall and started to climb.

113
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:46,159
His stomach was still swollen from last night's gorge. Groaning and complaining,

114
00:10:46,159 --> 00:10:49,040
he pulled himself slowly to the ceiling.

115
00:10:49,040 --> 00:10:53,520
He crept along till he reached the egg sack.

116
00:10:53,520 --> 00:10:59,279
Charlotte moved aside for him. She was dying, but she still had strength enough

117
00:10:59,279 --> 00:11:06,079
to move a little. Then Templeton bared his long, ugly teeth and began snipping

118
00:11:06,079 --> 00:11:10,559
the threads that fastened the sack to the ceiling.

119
00:11:10,559 --> 00:11:18,559
Wilbur watched from below. "Use extreme care," he said. "I don't want a single

120
00:11:18,559 --> 00:11:25,279
one of those eggs harmed." This rough sticks in my mouth, complained the rat.

121
00:11:25,279 --> 00:11:31,439
It's worse than caramel candy. But Templeton worked away at the job and

122
00:11:31,439 --> 00:11:35,520
managed to cut the sack a drift and carry it to the ground where he dropped

123
00:11:35,520 --> 00:11:42,079
it in front of Wilbur. Wilbur heaved a great sigh of relief.

124
00:11:42,079 --> 00:11:48,879
"Thank you, Templeton," he said. "I will never forget this as long as I live."

125
00:11:48,879 --> 00:11:54,398
Neither will I, said the rat, picking his teeth. I feel as though I'd eaten a

126
00:11:54,398 --> 00:11:58,559
spool of thread. Well, home we go.

127
00:11:58,559 --> 00:12:03,520
Templeton crept into the crate and buried himself in the straw. He got out

128
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:08,719
of sight just in time. Lurvy and John Arabel and Mr. Zuckerman came along at

129
00:12:08,719 --> 00:12:15,680
that moment, followed by Mrs. Arable and Mrs. Zuckerman and Avery and Fern.

130
00:12:15,680 --> 00:12:20,398
Wilbur had already decided how he would carry the egg sack. There was only one

131
00:12:20,398 --> 00:12:25,680
way possible. He carefully took the little bundle in his mouth and held it

132
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:29,680
there on top of his tongue. He remembered what Charlotte had told him,

133
00:12:29,680 --> 00:12:33,040
that the sack was waterproof and strong.

134
00:12:33,040 --> 00:12:38,159
It felt funny on his tongue and made him drool a bit, and of course he couldn't

135
00:12:38,159 --> 00:12:40,879
say anything.

136
00:12:40,879 --> 00:12:44,478
But as he was being shoved into the crate, he looked up at Charlotte and

137
00:12:44,478 --> 00:12:50,318
gave her a wink. She knew he was saying goodbye in the only way he could, and

138
00:12:50,318 --> 00:12:53,359
she knew her children were safe.

139
00:12:53,359 --> 00:13:00,000
"Goodbye," she whispered. Then she summoned all her strength and waved one

140
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,719
of her front legs at him.

141
00:13:02,719 --> 00:13:06,318
She never moved again.

142
00:13:06,318 --> 00:13:11,120
Next day, as the ferris wheel was being taken apart and the raceh horses were

143
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:14,879
being loaded into vans and the entertainers were packing up their

144
00:13:14,879 --> 00:13:21,120
belongings and driving away in their trailers, Charlotte died.

145
00:13:21,120 --> 00:13:26,398
The fairgrounds were soon deserted. The sheds and buildings were empty and

146
00:13:26,398 --> 00:13:32,639
forlorn. The infield was littered with bottles and trash. Nobody of the

147
00:13:32,639 --> 00:13:37,920
hundreds of people that had visited the fair knew that a gray spider had played

148
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:45,719
the most important part of all. No one was with her when she died.
